# Error Handling (facturador-crecer-api)

## try/catch

- Wrap async work that can fail (I/O, external APIs, persistence, parsing) in `try/catch`.
- In controllers and use cases, catch errors, log useful context, and rethrow domain/HTTP errors or return the proper response.
- Never use empty `catch` blocks. Never swallow errors silently.
- Prefer `async/await` with `try/catch` over `.catch()`.

```typescript
try {
  const receipt = await this.receiptCreator.run(payload);
  response.status(201).json(receipt);
} catch (error) {
  logger.error('Failed to create receipt', { error });
  next(error);
}
```

## Guidelines

- Use existing domain exceptions when they fit.
- Client-facing messages may be in Spanish; internal logs stay in English.
- Do not catch only to rethrow the same error with no added value unless required by a boundary (controller → middleware).
- Validate inputs early and fail fast with clear errors.
